 "chunks": [
  {
   "category": "study_plan",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Biomedical Engineering (الهندسة الطبية الحيوية) — B.Sc. study plan 2025/2026, Faculty of Engineering & Design, Middle East University.\nThe degree requires 162 credit hours in total:\n- University requirements: 18 credit hours (compulsory)\n- University electives: 6 credit hours\n- Faculty requirements: 24 credit hours (group A: 6, group B: 18 — mathematics, physics, chemistry)\n- Area of study (major) requirements: 61 credit hours\n- Ancillary (supporting) courses: 44 credit hours\n- Area of study (major) electives: 9 credit hours (three 3-hour courses chosen from nine)\nRemedial courses (Arabic, English, computer skills) are taken only when required and are not counted in the 162 hours.\nThe plan includes external Field Training (after 115 completed credit hours) and a two-part graduation project (Graduation Project I after 120 completed credit hours, then Graduation Project II)."
  },
  {
   "category": "study_plan",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Biomedical Engineering study plan 2025/2026 — approvals and signatories.\nFaculty Council decision 06/06-2025/2026, adopted 06/11/2025. Deans' Council decision 09/15-2025/2026, adopted 30/12/2025.\nDean of the Faculty: Prof. Ayman Abdel Salam Awad. Director of Admissions and Registration: Mrs. Nadia Al-Bakri."
  },
  {
   "category": "study_plan",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Biomedical Engineering — biomedical courses in the 2025/2026 study plan:\nBiochemistry (كيمياء حيوية, 1961601), Anatomy and Physiology (علم وظائف الأعضاء والتشريح, 1962601), Biomechanics (ميكانيكا حيوية, 1962602), Introduction to Biomedical Engineering (1962701), Biostatistics (1963401), Biomedical Signal Processing (معالجة الإشارة الطبية, 1963403), Biomaterials (مواد طبية حيوية, 1963601), Biofluid Mechanics with lab (1963602/1964601), Medical Electronics with lab (الإلكترونيات الطبية, 1963701/1963702), Biomedical Measurements (1964805), Biomedical Instruments with lab (الأجهزة الطبية الحيوية, 1964701/1964702), Medical Image Processing with lab (1964801/1964802), Biomedical Modeling with lab (1964803/1964804), Microcontrollers with lab (1965501/1965502), Biomedical Sensors with lab (المجسات الطبية الحيوية, 1965801/1965802), Medical Imaging (التصوير الطبي, 1965701).\nMajor electives (choose 9 credit hours): Artificial Intelligence in Medical Diagnosis, Bioinformatics, Bio-Signal Monitoring Systems (أنظمة المراقبة الحيوية), Medical Robots (الروبوتات الطبية), Prosthetics (الأطراف الصناعية), Tissue Engineering (هندسة الأنسجة), Biomedical Transition (الانتقال الطبي الحيوي), Management and Specifications of Medical Devices in Hospitals, Special Topics in Biomedical Engineering.\nSupporting engineering courses include electric circuits, electronics, digital logic design, signals and systems, control systems, engineering programming, numerical analysis and engineering mathematics."
  }
 ],
